You've at least three moves, and possibly four, before the mind flayer
can close and begin attacking thanks to the potion of speed you just
drank.  You are fire resistant, and holding onto a fire bomb (of sorts).

Throw the potion of oil at the mind flayer; the explosion will also
damage the gnome king.  (You could also bomb the gnome king, but this
would fire damage your inventory.)  Burning oil does 4d4 damage, which
could potentially kill the gnome king if you've already hit him a bit.

If the potion kills the gnome king, check if the mind flayer has had its
move yet.  If it has, you can make the two moves to the upstairs and
escape; if not you can wait for it to close and have a fairly high
chance of making those two moves as well.

If the potion does not kill the gnome king:
- If the mind flayer has not moved, zap the gnome king with the magic
  missile, which should kill him.  The mind flayer will probably get its
  move, meaning you will be able to make the two moves to get to the
  stairs.
- If the mind flayer has moved, it will be able to land at least one
  attack against you in two moves (fortunately you have enough HP left
  to survive its attacks).  Therefore you would again zap the gnome king
  with the wand of magic missile and attempt to flee for the stairs
  after he dies; you'll take some intelligence drain but should survive.
  


